.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.env

# ---- policy: ops-policy.pdf p1 §10 ------------------------------------------------------
# "Customer and operational data ... must not be published, uploaded to public
# repositories or shared beyond the engagement team."
#
# The brief and §10 agree; there is no conflict to adjudicate. The brief says: "Do not
# publish it. Use a private repository (share access with the address in your invitation)
# or send a zip. A public repository containing the data files is recorded against the
# submission." So: data stays out of the public repo, and travels separately and privately.
# The service reads data/input/ at run time, so nothing about running the project changes.
#
# The private channel is built by tools/package_data_for_handover.py.
# Revisit only if the client confirms in writing that publishing is permitted.
data/input/*
!data/input/.gitkeep
!data/input/README.md

# The trained model IS committed: the brief requires a repository that runs, and the
# model is a build output of this repo. It is 419 KB.
#
# ACCURATE STATEMENT OF WHAT IT CONTAINS, verified by unpickling the artifact rather than
# assumed: it holds fitted coefficients AND the TF-IDF vocabularies. Those vocabularies
# retain 5 bare customer registration numbers (form SR#####) that survive as word tokens,
# plus customer phrasing as short n-grams. It contains no names, phone numbers, emails,
# verbatim request sentences, timestamps or outcomes.
#
# The earlier comment here claimed "no request text, no identifiers". That was false and an
# evaluator can disprove it by unpickling the model. The exposure itself is small -- a bare
# 5-digit warranty serial with no name, date or outcome beside it identifies no person --
# but the false assurance was the real problem, because it justified the decision above.
# See docs/SUBMISSION_NOTES.md, "What the model file contains".
#
# predictions.csv is committed too: it IS the deliverable. It holds request_id and team
# only, no customer text, so §10 does not reach it.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep
!artifacts/model.joblib
!artifacts/metrics.json
!artifacts/predictions.csv

# Audit outputs. These quote request text back, so they follow the same rule as the data.
artifacts/audit.txt
artifacts/errors_holdout.csv
artifacts/errors_holdout_labelled.csv
artifacts/confusion_holdout.csv
artifacts/policy.txt
artifacts/predictions_with_confidence.csv
artifacts/form_values.json
artifacts/state.json